[Rendered.](https://github.com/varkor/rfcs/blob/bool-to-option/text/0000-bool-to-option.md)

The following pattern is prevalent in [typical Rust code](https://sourcegraph.com/search?q=repogroup%3Acrates+%2Felse%5Cs*%7B%5Cs*None%5Cs*%7D%2F+count%3A1000).

```rust 
if some_condition {
    Some(t)
} else {
    None
}
```

Here, I propose new methods for converting a `bool` to an `Option<T>`, abstracting this pattern, to aid in readability and reducing repetition.

```rust
impl bool {
    fn to_option<T>(self, t: T) -> Option<T>;
    fn to_option_with<T, F: FnOnce() -> T>(self, f: F) -> Option<T>;
}
```

This supersedes https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/2180, which was closed due to concerns about the suggested names and resolves https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/2606.

